## What it is

A competitive tactical shooter built around team objectives and round-based decisions.

## Before you install

Checked 23 November 2026. Steam lists Valve as developer and publisher. The release date it shows, 21 August 2012, belongs to store app 730, which Counter-Strike 2 now occupies, so it is not a Counter-Strike 2 launch date. The base game is free to play, with in-app purchases. The minimum column asks for Windows 10, a processor with 4 hardware threads (Intel Core i5 750 or higher), 8 GB of memory, a DirectX 11 graphics card with at least 1 GB and Shader Model 5.0 support, and 85 GB of storage. Valve Anti-Cheat is enabled, and Steam lists cross-platform multiplayer. Its content notice mentions intense violence and blood.

Counter-Strike 2 is a round-based tactical shooter, not a battle royale. Steam’s app details, checked 8 November 2026, list Windows and Linux for the free base game. Optional purchases and the current system requirements are on that same Steam page.

## Official installation and support

Follow the official store link above for installation and updates. GameNews does not host game files. If installation fails, record the error and your hardware details before consulting the publisher's support resources.

## Editorial basis

Researched from the [official Steam listing](https://store.steampowered.com/app/730/CounterStrike_2/) on 15 October 2026 and rechecked on 23 November 2026. This is a product overview, not a hands-on performance review. Selected using [Steam's most-played chart](https://store.steampowered.com/charts/mostplayed/); player activity is not search-volume data.
